PHASE 6C — REPLACE CUSTOM MCP PROTOCOL WITH OFFICIAL MCP C# SDK

The current NovaBanking.McpServer implementation is NOT using the official MCP SDK.

It currently implements custom endpoints:

GET  /mcp/discover
POST /mcp/invoke

This is a custom HTTP tool protocol, not the actual Model Context Protocol.

We need to replace the custom protocol with the official Microsoft-collaborated MCP C# SDK.

Use the official package:

ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore

This is an ASP.NET Core HTTP MCP server and the official SDK supports HTTP-based MCP servers.

Reference:
https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/csharp-sdk

==================================================
CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS
==================================================

DO NOT change the existing banking domain/service architecture.

Keep:

MCP tool
    ↓
IBankingService
    ↓
ICurrentUserAccessor
    ↓
NB_SID server-side session
    ↓
CustomerId
    ↓
ownership check
    ↓
Azure SQL

The MCP tools must NEVER accept CustomerId as an authorization parameter.

Do NOT query EF Core directly from MCP tools.

Do NOT bypass BankingService.

Do NOT trust CustomerId supplied by an LLM/client.

Do NOT hardcode CustomerId.

==================================================
1. INSTALL OFFICIAL MCP SDK
==================================================

Add the appropriate official NuGet package:

ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore

Use the current stable version compatible with the project's target framework.

Do NOT install unofficial MCP packages.

Do NOT implement the MCP wire protocol manually.

Do NOT create another custom /mcp/discover or /mcp/invoke protocol.

==================================================
2. IMPLEMENT REAL MCP SERVER
==================================================

Configure NovaBanking.McpServer using the official MCP ASP.NET Core integration.

Use:

AddMcpServer()

and the appropriate HTTP transport configuration for the current SDK version.

Use the SDK's actual MCP transport endpoint.

Do not create a custom JSON transport.

The server must support genuine MCP client discovery and tool invocation.

==================================================
3. MCP TOOLS
==================================================

Create actual MCP server tools using the official SDK's tool registration mechanism.

Expose exactly:

GetCustomerProfile()
GetAccountSummary()
GetAccountBalance(accountId)
GetRecentTransactions(accountId, count)
GetLoanSummary(loanId)
GetCreditCardSummary(cardId)

Use the SDK's McpServerTool / McpServerToolType mechanism or the current equivalent for the installed SDK version.

Each tool must have:
- proper MCP tool name
- description
- parameter schema
- structured output
- read-only behavior

Use Description attributes where appropriate so the SDK generates correct tool metadata/schema.

==================================================
4. BANKING SERVICE
==================================================

Each MCP tool must call IBankingService.

Example conceptual flow:

[MCP GetAccountBalance]
        ↓
IBankingService.GetAccountBalanceAsync(accountId)
        ↓
ICurrentUserAccessor
        ↓
authenticated CustomerId
        ↓
ownership predicate
        ↓
Azure SQL

Do not duplicate banking logic in the MCP layer.

==================================================
5. AUTHENTICATION
==================================================

Preserve the existing NB_SID server-side session architecture.

The MCP request must be associated with an authenticated customer context.

The MCP layer must not accept:

customerId

as a tool parameter.

The resource IDs such as accountId, loanId and cardId are only selectors.

BankingService remains responsible for checking ownership.

If the official MCP HTTP transport has a request/HttpContext integration mechanism, use it to access the existing authenticated context.

If the MCP SDK's transport changes how HttpContext is exposed, implement the minimal secure adapter needed for ICurrentUserAccessor.

Do NOT weaken authentication to make MCP work.

==================================================
6. REMOVE CUSTOM PROTOCOL
==================================================

Remove or disable the custom:

McpProtocolController
/mcp/discover
/mcp/invoke

implementation.

Do not leave two competing MCP implementations.

The final NovaBanking.McpServer should have ONE real MCP implementation.

The old McpToolsController may also be removed if it is only duplicate REST tooling and is no longer needed.

Do not remove BankingService or any application-layer functionality.

==================================================
7. TESTING
==================================================

Update tests to test the actual MCP implementation rather than testing the custom controller.

Tests must verify:

- MCP server starts
- MCP client can connect using the supported HTTP transport
- MCP tool discovery returns all six tools
- GetCustomerProfile works
- GetAccountSummary works
- GetAccountBalance works
- GetRecentTransactions works
- GetLoanSummary works
- GetCreditCardSummary works
- unauthenticated requests are rejected
- another customer's resources cannot be accessed
- CustomerId cannot be supplied to override authenticated identity
- sensitive data is not exposed

Use the official SDK's testing/client facilities where practical.

Do not merely unit-test a custom controller.

==================================================
8. BUILD / TEST
==================================================

Run:

dotnet build

dotnet test

Fix all compilation and test failures.

